N5008 [expr.prim.id.unqual]/4, [expr.ref]/6.3.1: a static member function,
named unqualified or by a class member access, is an lvalue of function type,
which converts to a pointer ([conv.func]); a cast of it was rejected as a use
of a non-static member function, and the member access was no lvalue.
